# Verbara cosign public key (ECDSA P-256).
#
# Customer-facing verification of all signed images under ghcr.io/verbara/platform/*.
# This file is served verbatim from https://verbara.io/keys/cosign.pub and is the
# canonical public reference for the keypair that signs:
#   - ghcr.io/verbara/platform/api:vX.Y.Z         (Native AOT — Pro IP)
#   - ghcr.io/verbara/platform/realtime:vX.Y.Z    (SignalR Hub microservice)
#   - ghcr.io/verbara/platform/renderer:vX.Y.Z    (PDF/CSV renderer)
#   - ghcr.io/verbara/platform/mail:vX.Y.Z        (SMTP/MS Graph outbound)
#   - ghcr.io/verbara/platform/web:vX.Y.Z-web     (React frontend bundle)
#
# Verify any pulled image:
#   cosign verify --key https://verbara.io/keys/cosign.pub --insecure-ignore-tlog \
#     ghcr.io/verbara/platform/api:v2.4.2
#
# The same key is committed in the source repos as `.github/cosign.pub` and
# `docker/cosign.pub` — operators preferring an independent channel can `diff`
# the served file against the in-repo copy:
#   curl -sL https://verbara.io/keys/cosign.pub | diff - docker/cosign.pub
#
# Private-key custody and rotation procedure: see
# Verbara.Sdk.Pro/docs/operations/2026-05-10-cosign-keypair-bootstrap.md.
#
# Verbara signing posture: `--tlog-upload=false` (skips Rekor transparency log),
# documented in customer manuales. Verification consumers must pass
# `--insecure-ignore-tlog` to match. See ADR-0023 (Verbara.Platform repo) for
# the full IP-protection layering rationale.
-----BEGIN PUBLIC KEY-----
MFkwEwYHKoZIzj0CAQYIKoZIzj0DAQcDQgAEBKvVcEKiEr1VKAlS2tnnaBOymdBY
Il+bfvD2YMK7KQe+QdziuA1dVa8TGmg0NGM082ScomxlxxNI8aMRAGN0aQ==
-----END PUBLIC KEY-----
